IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`
IMPORT `scja1-part1-preliminary`

-- Tests for scja1-part1-preliminary.l4 (s 2). Expected values are written from the text of s 2 (SCJA1969.txt lines 378-433), not from the code.

§ `Fixtures`

`a Chief Justice` MEANS Judge OF "CJ", `Chief Justice`, Date 11 4 2012
`a Vice-President of the Court of Appeal` MEANS Judge OF "VP", `Vice-President of the Court of Appeal`, Date 1 1 2014
`a Justice of the Court of Appeal` MEANS Judge OF "JA", `Justice of the Court of Appeal`, Date 1 1 2015
`the President of the Appellate Division` MEANS Judge OF "PAD", `President of the Appellate Division`, Date 1 1 2016
`a Judge of the Appellate Division` MEANS Judge OF "JAD", `Judge of the Appellate Division`, Date 2 1 2017
`a Judge of the High Court` MEANS Judge OF "J", `Judge of the High Court`, Date 3 1 2018
`a Judicial Commissioner` MEANS Judge OF "JC", `Judicial Commissioner`, Date 4 1 2019
`a Senior Judge` MEANS Judge OF "SJ", `Senior Judge`, Date 5 1 2020
`an International Judge` MEANS Judge OF "IJ", `International Judge`, Date 6 1 2021

§§ `s 2 opening words: unless the context otherwise requires`

-- The context requires otherwise: the text says the definitions do not govern then ("unless"): FALSE. Otherwise they govern: TRUE.
#ASSERT (`s 2 the definitions of this section govern the word here` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 2 the definitions of this section govern the word here` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 2 "Appellate Division" and "court" and "Family Division of the High Court" and "General Division"`

#ASSERT (`s 2 Appellate Division: the court is the Appellate Division of the High Court` `Appellate Division`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 2 Appellate Division: the court is the Appellate Division of the High Court` `General Division`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 2 Appellate Division: the court is the Appellate Division of the High Court` `Court of Appeal`) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- "court" means the General Division, the Appellate Division, or the Court of Appeal.
#ASSERT (`s 2 court: the court is the General Division, the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` `General Division`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 2 court: the court is the General Division, the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` `Appellate Division`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 2 court: the court is the General Division, the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` `Court of Appeal`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 2 court: the court is the General Division, the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` `District Court`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 2 court: the court is the General Division, the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` `Family Division of the High Court`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The Singapore International Commercial Court is a division of the General Division (s 18A); s 2 does not name it: NOTHING.
#ASSERT (`s 2 court: the court is the General Division, the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` `Singapore International Commercial Court`) EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT (`s 2 Family Division of the High Court: the court is the Family Division of the High Court` `Family Division of the High Court`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 2 Family Division of the High Court: the court is the Family Division of the High Court` `General Division`) EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT (`s 2 General Division: the court is the General Division of the High Court` `General Division`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 2 General Division: the court is the General Division of the High Court` `Appellate Division`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 2 General Division: the court is the General Division of the High Court` `Singapore International Commercial Court`) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 2 "Family Justice Rules"`

#ASSERT (`s 2 Family Justice Rules: the instrument is the Family Justice Rules` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 2 Family Justice Rules: the instrument is the Family Justice Rules` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 2 Family Justice Rules: the instrument is the Family Justice Rules` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 2 "Supreme Court Judge" and "Judge"`

-- "Supreme Court Judge" means the Chief Justice, a Justice of the Court of Appeal, a Judge of the Appellate Division or a Judge of the High Court.
#ASSERT (`s 2 Supreme Court Judge: the person is a Supreme Court Judge` `a Chief Justice`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 2 Supreme Court Judge: the person is a Supreme Court Judge` `a Justice of the Court of Appeal`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 2 Supreme Court Judge: the person is a Supreme Court Judge` `a Vice-President of the Court of Appeal`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 2 Supreme Court Judge: the person is a Supreme Court Judge` `a Judge of the Appellate Division`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 2 Supreme Court Judge: the person is a Supreme Court Judge` `the President of the Appellate Division`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 2 Supreme Court Judge: the person is a Supreme Court Judge` `a Judge of the High Court`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The Judge definition lists a Judicial Commissioner, a Senior Judge and an International Judge beside a Supreme Court Judge, so they are not one.
#ASSERT (`s 2 Supreme Court Judge: the person is a Supreme Court Judge` `a Judicial Commissioner`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 2 Supreme Court Judge: the person is a Supreme Court Judge` `a Senior Judge`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 2 Supreme Court Judge: the person is a Supreme Court Judge` `an International Judge`) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- "Judge" means a Supreme Court Judge, a Judicial Commissioner, a Senior Judge or an International Judge: every office of the core is one of them.
#ASSERT (`s 2 Judge: the person is a Supreme Court Judge, a Judicial Commissioner, a Senior Judge or an International Judge` `a Chief Justice`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 2 Judge: the person is a Supreme Court Judge, a Judicial Commissioner, a Senior Judge or an International Judge` `a Judicial Commissioner`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 2 Judge: the person is a Supreme Court Judge, a Judicial Commissioner, a Senior Judge or an International Judge` `a Senior Judge`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 2 Judge: the person is a Supreme Court Judge, a Judicial Commissioner, a Senior Judge or an International Judge` `an International Judge`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 2 Judge: the person is a Supreme Court Judge, a Judicial Commissioner, a Senior Judge or an International Judge` `a Judge of the High Court`) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- limbs (a), (b), (c): a Judge sitting in that Division / Court in accordance with the Constitution and the Act; otherwise not ("means").
#ASSERT (`s 2 Judge (a): in relation to the General Division, the person is a Judge sitting in that Division` `a Judge of the High Court` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 2 Judge (a): in relation to the General Division, the person is a Judge sitting in that Division` `a Judge of the High Court` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 2 Judge (b): in relation to the Appellate Division, the person is a Judge sitting in that Division` `a Judge of the Appellate Division` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 2 Judge (b): in relation to the Appellate Division, the person is a Judge sitting in that Division` `a Judge of the Appellate Division` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 2 Judge (c): in relation to the Court of Appeal, the person is a Judge sitting in that Court` `a Justice of the Court of Appeal` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 2 Judge (c): in relation to the Court of Appeal, the person is a Judge sitting in that Court` `a Justice of the Court of Appeal` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 2 Judge (c): in relation to the Court of Appeal, the person is a Judge sitting in that Court` `an International Judge` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `s 2 "Registrar", "Rules of Court", "seal"`

#ASSERT (`s 2 Registrar: the officer is the Registrar, the Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar` Registrar) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 2 Registrar: the officer is the Registrar, the Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar` `Deputy Registrar`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 2 Registrar: the officer is the Registrar, the Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar` `Assistant Registrar`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "includes" leaves the list open: another officer is not covered.
#ASSERT (`s 2 Registrar: the officer is the Registrar, the Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar` Sheriff) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 2 Registrar: the officer is the Registrar, the Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar` Clerk) EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT (`s 2 Rules of Court: the instrument is Rules of Court made under this Act or a form` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 2 Rules of Court: the instrument is Rules of Court made under this Act or a form` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 2 Rules of Court: the instrument is Rules of Court made under this Act or a form` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT (`s 2 seal: the thing is a seal or a stamp` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 2 seal: the thing is a seal or a stamp` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 2 seal: the thing is a seal or a stamp` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 2 "subordinate court"`

-- District Court and Magistrate's Court (State Courts Act 1970), Family Court and Youth Court (Family Justice Act 2014): named.
#ASSERT (`s 2 subordinate court: the court is a subordinate court` `District Court` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 2 subordinate court: the court is a subordinate court` `Magistrate's Court` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 2 subordinate court: the court is a subordinate court` `Family Court` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 2 subordinate court: the court is a subordinate court` `Youth Court` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Any other court or tribunal: it depends on a written-law right of appeal to the Supreme Court; without one, not ("means").
#ASSERT (`s 2 subordinate court: the court is a subordinate court` `Syariah Court` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 2 subordinate court: the court is a subordinate court` `Syariah Court` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 2 subordinate court: the court is a subordinate court` `another subordinate court, tribunal or judicial or quasi-judicial body` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 2 subordinate court: the court is a subordinate court` `another subordinate court, tribunal or judicial or quasi-judicial body` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A division of the Supreme Court itself: not answered.
#ASSERT (`s 2 subordinate court: the court is a subordinate court` `General Division` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 2 subordinate court: the court is a subordinate court` `Court of Appeal` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
